cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dy-wcet: worst-case response time in integer arithmetic"
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yermakou"
    given-names: "Denis"
    email: "connect@axonos.org"
    affiliation: "DY Research"
abstract: >-
  Response-time analysis for fixed-priority task sets with release jitter and
  blocking, computed entirely in integer arithmetic over the level-i busy
  period, so that a task whose response runs past its own period is charged for
  the self-interference that follows. Non-convergence returns an
  explicit unbounded result rather than a capped value, a bound above the
  deadline is reported with its value rather than discarded, and every
  operation is checked so that overflow cannot turn an unschedulable set into a
  schedulable-looking one. Includes Audsley's optimal priority assignment.
repository-code: "https://github.com/DYResearch/dy-wcet"
url: "https://github.com/DYResearch/dy-wcet"
version: "4.1.3"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: "Apache-2.0 OR MIT"
keywords:
  - real-time systems
  - response-time analysis
  - fixed-priority scheduling
  - worst-case execution time
  - release jitter
  - embedded

